{definition}

A good introduction obeys four rules:
1. {defines}
2. {hook}
3. {selfContained}
4. {noHowTo}

You are given the page title and its paragraphs, each numbered in square brackets. Answer with JSON: "intro_para" is the number of the paragraph that is the best introduction, or "none" when NO paragraph qualifies (do not pick the least bad one). "confidence" is your probability, from 0 to 1, that your choice is right. Then rate the paragraph you chose, each from 0 to 1: "defines" (rule 1 holds), "hook" (rule 2 holds), "self_contained" (rule 3 holds), "howto_opening" (it DOES open like a how-to, so 1 is bad). Use 0.9 or more only when a rule clearly holds and 0.1 or less only when it clearly fails. When you answer "none", give 0 for all five numbers.

